    "body": "### Problem\n\nEnter, tab, and backspace are processed twice in normal, insert, and command modes in the kitty terminal. \nNeovim 0.11.5 in kitty does NOT reproduce it\nTerminator + Neovim 0.12.4 stable does NOT reproduce it\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\ncurl -LO https://github.com/neovim/neovim/releases/latest/download/nvim-linux-x86_64.appimage\nchmod +x nvim-linux-x86_64.appimage\nsudo mv nvim-linux-x86_64.appimage /usr/local/bin/nvim\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIn insert mode, the text should look like this:\n```\nI lost\nthe \ngame\n```\nBut looks like \n```\nI lost\n\nthe\n\ngame\n```\nBackspacing at the end should look like `gam` but looks like `ga`\nIn normal mode, backspace should go left 1 char but goes back two\nIn normal mode, enter should go down one line but goes down two\nIn insert mode, tab should insert one tab but inserts two\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1251+g5117b04745\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.1\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nPopOS 24.04\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.32.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nappimage",
